[Player:Charlie the Chef]
Charlie is drawn in #COLOUR$47. The two walking frames are twenty pixels tall,
and include the chef's hat.
#UDGTABLE(default,centre,centre)
  { =h Frame 1 | =h Frame 2 }
  { #N$01 | #N$02 }
  { #SPRITE$01,attr=$47(charlie-01-colour*)
    | #SPRITE$02,attr=$47(charlie-02-colour*) }
UDGTABLE#

#FRAMES(charlie-01-colour,20;charlie-02-colour)(charlie-colour)

[Player:Charlie Losing A Life]
When Charlie is touched by a nasty or an ingredient his sprite is replaced by
the hatless body (#N$0C). The hat (#N$0D) floats up the screen, and Charlie
(#N$0E) then falls down it.
#UDGTABLE(default,centre,centre,centre)
  { =h Hatless | =h Hat | =h Falling }
  { #N$0C | #N$0D | #N$0E }
  { #SPRITE$0C,attr=$47(charlie-hatless-colour)
    | #SPRITE$0D,attr=$47(charlie-hat-colour)
    | #SPRITE$0E,attr=$47(charlie-falling-colour) }
UDGTABLE#

[Player:Flour]
Charlie throws these in #COLOUR$47. The explosion is shown when a shot reaches
the edge of the playing area, or hits a nasty.
#UDGTABLE(default,centre,centre,centre)
  { =h Flour Shot | =h Explosion Frame 1 | =h Explosion Frame 2 }
  { #N$03 | #N$26 | #N$27 }
  { #SPRITE$03,attr=$47(flour-colour)
    | #SPRITE$26,attr=$47(explosion-01-colour*)
    | #SPRITE$27,attr=$47(explosion-02-colour*) }
UDGTABLE#

#FRAMES(explosion-02-colour,50;explosion-01-colour)(explosion-colour)

